% Abstract
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\begin{abstract}
%\boldmath
This paper presents the design of a database management system for Katikafwe Private School with the aim of improving the management of academic and administrative records. The school faces challenges in tracking information across twelve grades, each divided into two classes, with additional complexity arising from the management of students, teachers, subjects, and guardians.

The system was developed through a structured process that involves requirement analysis, conceptual design, logical design, and physical implementation. Conceptual modeling used a standard ER notation and Crow’s Foot notation to represent entities, attributes, relationships, and constraints, while also incorporating multivalued, composite, and derived attributes. The logical design was implemented in MySQL to provide reliable data storage, accurate performance tracking, and simplified report generation.

The resulting framework strengthens the management of records at Katikafwe Private School and provides a scalable foundation for future integration with a full school information system.

 


\end{abstract}
