%% INTRODUCTION
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Introduction}

The management of modern educational institutions requires more advanced data capturing systems that are very fast but maintain a certain degree of accuracy. Katikafwe Private School, which enrolls students from grade one to grade twelve, faces challenges in managing its academic records due to their reliance in traditional record-keeping methods. The school’s operational records include twelve distinct grade levels each with exactly two classes, teacher assignments across various roles, mandatory and selective subjects, student enrollment records, guardian records, and academic performance tracking across multiple assessments.

Traditional methods such as spreadsheets and paper-based systems are increasingly inadequate for handling these complexities. Reason being, they often result in data redundancy, inconsistencies, and difficulty in generating accurate reports as well as retrieving them. Katikafwe Private School’s specific requirements in addition to the ones mentioned earlier include maintaining exactly two classes per grade, managing hierarchical teacher roles, ensuring students enroll in all mandatory subjects while selecting electives, guarantee of each student to have at least one guardian, and tracking term-based test results.

This paper presents the design and implementation of a comprehensive relational database system which is developed to address the challenges faced by the institution. The methodology used was Agile-informed waterfall model. This model structured the project into four distinct phases which include: the requirements analysis, conceptual modeling using Entity-Relationship (ER) diagrams, logical design into a normalized relational schema, and physical implementation in MySQL. This hybrid approach combined the systematic progression of traditional waterfall development with iterative refinement cycles characteristic of Agile methodologies, ensuring thorough validation at each development stage /cite\{Pargaonkar\}. The resulting database system not only meets the institution's current operational requirements but also ensures a dynamic system scalable for the future institutional growth. Ultimately this enhances administrative efficiency, ensuring data integrity, and facilitating comprehensive academic monitoring capabilities for Katikafwe Private School

 

